  "details": "I am encountering video players seemingly downloading videos, finding video info and showing timestamp, and on most players showing the first frame, but the video never plays proper. \nRepro Steps: Place any video link in a video player.\nExpected: Video plays normally.\nActual: Above mentioned behavior.\nI have tried the following debug steps:\n- Ensured drivers and Windows both are updated.\n- Ensured vendor-provided codecs are installed.\n- Ensured all certificates unexpired and installed.\n- Ensured my game is not modified in any way.\n- Reset game cache.\n- Disabled and reenabled Untrusted URLs.\n- Reinstalled VRChat.\n- Ensured proper YTDLP is being found by VRChat.\n- Ensured there are no captcha issues.\n- Ensured there are no issues receiving the video through my firewall and connection.\n- Attempted this on both Flatscreen and VR modes.\n- Attempted troubleshooting via audio output configurations.\n- Confirmed there are no issues with my Nvidia configuration.\n- Ensured monitor resolution mismatch has not affected me in any way.\nThis issue is pervasive and has eluded both VRChat support and most community creators and advice. No advice given has helped, although I will happily try any obscure troubleshooting tips provided for thoroughness, and document anything that someone reminds me of.\nThis persists across all media sources, as well as across Unity Video and AVPro based players, as based on testing in the Video Player Showroom. \nBased on all information, I believe this to be a genuine bug.\nVideo: https://youtu.be/stt_4Nm6XAk (Audio from web browser tab)\nOutput Log: https://paste.gg/p/anonymous/66ecc0cf39f54bb0a5f0dbc495f865d8",
